					<h1 class="title" title="Andaman and Nicobar">Andaman and Nicobar</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">
    
   <p class="MsoNormal">
        <span>Andaman and Nicobar is a lovely place to visit with so many things to see. 
        There are around 500 islands spreading across the total distance of 780 Kms. The 
        Andaman groups of islands are originally populated by the Great Andamanese, the 
        Onge, the Jarawa and the Sentinelese. Port Blair is the capital of Andaman and 
        Nicobar. The Andaman and
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        Nicobar islands</st1:place> are renowned for the pristine clean coral beaches. 
        The Andaman &amp; Nicobar group is a cluster of islands that are a union
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placetype
 w:st="on">
        territory</st1:PlaceType> of
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        India</st1:PlaceName></st1:place> and are situated in the
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        Bay of Bengal</st1:place>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
        <span>The various places which can be visited in Andaman and
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        Nicobar Islands</st1:place> are:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <h3>City trip:</h3>
    One of the best places to visit in city is 
        Cellular jail, and others are Fisheries Museum, Andaman water sports complex, 
        Samudrika-Marine museum, Anthropological Museum, Forest museum, Mini zoo, Khadi 
        gramodoyg Emporium, Gandhi Park, Corbyn’s cove beach.&nbsp;<p class="MsoNormal">
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        </st1:place>
        <span> &nbsp;It’s a 
        half an hour journey from the city. Main interest in this island is the open 
        space jail also called Women jail.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
        <b><span>Chirya tapoo:</span></b><span> Also known as
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placename
 w:st="on">
        Bird</st1:PlaceName>
        <st1:placetype w:st="on">
        Island</st1:PlaceType></st1:place> and has a Bird Sanctuary.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
        <b><span>Mount Harriet:</span></b><span> The highest hill around South Andaman 
        (365m), lying on the other side of
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        Ross</st1:PlaceName>
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        Island</st1:PlaceName></st1:place>, provides an excellent view of the
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placetype w:st="on">
        Port</st1:PlaceType>
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        Blair</st1:PlaceName>
        <st1:placetype w:st="on">
        City</st1:PlaceType></st1:place>.
        <br />
        <br />
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        <b>Neil</b></st1:PlaceName><b>
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        Island</st1:PlaceName></b></st1:place><b>:</b> A long shallow beach basically 
        used for timbering operations.<br />
        <br />
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        <b>Chatam</b></st1:PlaceName><b>
        <st1:placetype w:st="on">
        Island</st1:PlaceType></b></st1:place><b>:</b> It is the center of activity of 
        the Forest Department. It has perhaps the biggest Saw Mill Tours to some of the 
        Andaman and
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        Nicobar islands</st1:place>, which are open to of its kind in
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        Asia</st1:place>.<br />
        <br />
        <b>Kondul:</b> It is a small island to the north of Great Nicobar and is known 
        for good canoes.<br />
        <br />
        <b>Katchal:</b> It is the most developed island. Scheduled tribe forms the major 
        part of the population. The soil is most suitable for Rubber Plantation.<br />
        <br />
        <b>Pullomillor:</b> It an extremely beautiful island known for copra and betel 
        nut plantation.<br />
        <br />
        <b>Madhuban:</b> &nbsp;The land is used as a training ground for elephants by 
        rangers.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
        <st1:city w:st="on">
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <b><span>North Bay</span></b></st1:place></st1:City><b><span>:</span></b><span> 
        This beach is 15 to 20 minutes journey by sea from Phoenix Bay Jetty at Port 
        blair.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        <b><span>Ross</span></b></st1:PlaceName><b><span>
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        Island</st1:PlaceName></span></b></st1:place><b><span>:</span></b><span> It used 
        to be a British colony where had lived. This is just 30 minutes sea journey from 
        Phoenix Bay Jetty of Port Blair.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
        <b><span>Red skin
        <st1:place
w:st="on">
        Island</st1:place>:</span></b><span> &nbsp;Situated in Mahatma Gandhi Marine national 
        park and is famous for under water corals and marine life.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        <b><span>Havelock</span></b></st1:PlaceName><b><span>
        <st1:placetype w:st="on">
        Island</st1:PlaceType></span></b></st1:place><b><span>:</span></b><span> This is 
        a very famous beach for its golden sand and bluish sea water.<br />
        &nbsp;<br />
        <b>Baratang:</b> Located at Middle Andaman. The journey is through thick, dense 
        forest area.<br />
        &nbsp;<br />
        Limestone caves near Baratang jetty, Mud Volcano, Rangat, Chidiyatapu (Place for 
        Sun set); Hut bay islands are the other places to see.
        <o:p>
        </o:p>
        </span>
    </p>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
        <span>In short we can say Andaman and
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        Nicobar islands</st1:place> comprises of 572 bright emerald islands, atolls and 
        rocks.
        <st1:place w:st="on">
        <st1:placename
 w:st="on">
        Mahatma</st1:PlaceName>
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        Gandhi</st1:PlaceName>
        <st1:placename w:st="on">
        Marine</st1:PlaceName>
        <st1:placetype w:st="on">
        National Park</st1:PlaceType></st1:place> is one of the unique places to be 
        visited. Madhuban is the most diverse forms of unusual birds, butterflies and 
        animals. Ramnagar beach is one of the beautiful beaches. For tourists these 
        places are a feast to the eyes with their lush green flora, exquisite fauna, 
        lovely beaches and widespread lagoons enclosed by exotic coral reefs. Thus we 
        can say there is another paradise on earth.&nbsp;
<a href="https://www.indiacitytrip.com/andaman-and-nicobar-destinations/">Andaman and Nicobar destinations and islands</a>
        <o:p>
        </o:p>
        </span>
    </p>

    
